## Summary of Changes

### 1. `MetadataDriftDetected` Event (PRD-05 §4.4)

**`crates/polkagent-core/src/event.rs`** — Added `MetadataDriftDetected` variant to `EventKind`:
- Fields: `chain_id`, `pinned_hash`, `current_hash`
- Durable durability

**`crates/polkagent-event/src/types.rs`** — Added `MetadataDriftDetected` to the `EventType` catalog:
- `as_str()` → `"metadata_drift_detected"`
- `from_kind()` mapping from `EventKind::MetadataDriftDetected`
- Default durability: `Durable`

**`crates/polkagent-telemetry/src/jsonl.rs`** — Added match arm for `MetadataDriftDetected`

### 2. `MetadataDriftWatcher` Background Service

**`crates/polkagent-service/src/metadata_watcher.rs`** (new file) — Background watcher that:
- Polls `MetadataService::check_drift()` on configured chain IDs at a configurable interval
- Publishes `MetadataDriftDetected` events to the `EventBus` when drift is found
- Follows the `WebhookDispatcher` pattern: `new()` → `start()` → `shutdown()`
- Uses `tokio::select!` with `watch::channel` for clean shutdown
- Is **detect-and-propose only** — never auto-merges metadata
- Includes `check_drift_all()` utility for on-demand checks (used by doctor)
- 6 unit tests covering: drift detection, event publishing, start/shutdown lifecycle

### 3. Wired into `AppService` and Startup

**`crates/polkagent-service/src/app.rs`**:
- `AppServiceBuilder::with_metadata_watcher()` builder method
- `metadata_watcher` field on `AppService` (Mutex-wrapped optional)
- `AppService::start_metadata_watcher()` — starts the watcher if configured
- Updated `Debug` impl to include `has_metadata_watcher`

**`crates/polkagent-service/src/lib.rs`**:
- Registered `metadata_watcher` module
- Re-exported `MetadataDriftWatcher`

**`crates/polkagent-service/Cargo.toml`** — Added `polkagent-metadata` dependency

### 4. `polkagent doctor` Metadata Drift Check

**`crates/polkagent-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs`** — Added `check_metadata_drift()`:
- Checks well-known chains (polkadot, kusama) for drift
- Reports `OK` when no drift, `WARN` per chain with drift details
- Appears in the system checks section alongside database/config/signer checks

**`crates/polkagent-cli/Cargo.toml`** — Added `polkagent-metadata` dependency

### 5. TUI Audit Tab Drift Alerts

**`crates/polkagent-cli/src/tui/db.rs`** — Updated severity classification to tag events with `kind` containing `"drift"` as `"warn"` severity (amber ▲ in the audit log)

**`crates/polkagent-cli/src/commands/run_printer.rs`** — Added match arm for `MetadataDriftDetected` to render drift warnings in CLI run output

